  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463168",
      "title": "Working with Event Arguments",
      "lectureOrder": 25,
      "videoOrder": 21,
      "sourceHash": "f9f65059d209b0d9ae390744d2f858defcafafe4ba7a3d4501d9141776f69a61",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "Okay. So we learned quite a bit about events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 9.95,
          "en": "What if we now don't just want to add one and subtract one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.08,
          "end": 14.28,
          "en": "but we want to be able to add five and reduce this by five?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.28,
          "end": 17.43,
          "en": "Maybe name it Subtract therefore, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 21.06,
          "en": "But the goal is that we now don't just add and deduct one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.06,
          "end": 23.663,
          "en": "but instead five, how would we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.99,
          "end": 26.99,
          "en": "Well, we of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.99,
          "end": 31.63,
          "en": "could accept a parameter in those methods, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.63,
          "end": 34.76,
          "en": "That is how we would probably do it in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.76,
          "end": 39.61,
          "en": "We can accept a parameter, number, or number, or n,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.61,
          "end": 40.69,
          "en": "totally up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.69,
          "end": 43.653,
          "en": "it's your method so you can accept whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.56,
          "end": 49.56,
          "en": "And then we could add num here or reduce num.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.71,
          "end": 52.86,
          "en": "Of course, we could also make this less dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.86,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "and just hard-code five here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 58.41,
          "en": "The problem just is that whenever we plan to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.41,
          "end": 61.93,
          "en": "change this number, we need to change it down there in code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.93,
          "end": 64.25,
          "en": "So it typically would be better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.25,
          "end": 66.58,
          "en": "to have a more dynamic method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.58,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "which gets the number which we wanna add or remove,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 74.14,
          "en": "and then uses this as a parameter like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.14,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "Then these methods will never need to be changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 82.3,
          "en": "when we decide to deduct or add a different number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.3,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "So that's the more generic and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 86.793,
          "en": "typically better way of writing these methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.94,
          "end": 90.76,
          "en": "But how do we tell Vue that it should call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.76,
          "end": 94.78,
          "en": "add and reduce with a value of five",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.78,
          "end": 97.31,
          "en": "for these parameters?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.31,
          "end": 98.71000000000001,
          "en": "Well, keep in mind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.71000000000001,
          "end": 102.65,
          "en": "we can execute add like this by pointing at it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.65,
          "end": 105.28999999999999,
          "en": "or by calling it explicitly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.28999999999999,
          "end": 109.84,
          "en": "Well, and if we called it like this, we're as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.84,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "in full control over the value we wanna pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 115.93,
          "en": "to the parameters of these methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.93,
          "end": 118.42,
          "en": "So here we can add five for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.42,
          "end": 121.68,
          "en": "and reduce by five, just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.68,
          "end": 124.67,
          "en": "And now whenever we decide to go for a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.67,
          "end": 128.36,
          "en": "we just have to change it here in HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.36,
          "end": 132.098,
          "en": "where we're changing the caption of the button anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.098,
          "end": 135.2,
          "en": "and the method will work correctly automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.2,
          "end": 137.733,
          "en": "because it's written in a very generic way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.49,
          "end": 141.61,
          "en": "So if we now save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.61,
          "end": 146.61,
          "en": "I can add 10 and subtract five and it just works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 151.88,
          "en": "So passing arguments to methods is also possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.88,
          "end": 153.3,
          "en": "and it's very easy to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "and this is an important pattern to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 159.56,
          "en": "This is important to understand, because in reality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.56,
          "end": 161.87,
          "en": "in apps you're building with Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.87,
          "end": 163.84,
          "en": "you will sometimes have the scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.84,
          "end": 166.43,
          "en": "that your method needs to get some parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.43,
          "end": 168.52,
          "en": "which you as a developer want to set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.52,
          "end": 171.61,
          "en": "and as you see, setting it and telling Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.61,
          "end": 176.61,
          "en": "to call this method with this value is super, super easy.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
